{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787919338987,"sessionID":"ses_fb7b4a8d5ffeJWKjfWHud2qnLO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_b5a9a6a6e24d45ff9e4a049d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/6kbt43_set-default-branch-in-settings/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/6kbt43_set-default-branch-in-settings/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: Set default branch in settings\n2: \n3: id: 6kbt43\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: @analyst\n6: date: 2026-08-11\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md, revised after human decisions. -->\n9: \n10: ## Scope summary\n11: \n12: Make the base branch (hardcoded as `main`) user-configurable, defaulting to\n13: `main`, so projects on `develop`/`master`/`trunk` can use the TUI. Per human\n14: decision #2, the base branch lives in a **project-scoped settings file**\n15: (`docs/manigot.json`), not the global TUI settings — base branch is a shared\n16: project convention, so it travels with the project (committable) and is read\n17: by both the TUI and the bare CLI `mg job`.\n18: \n19: ### Architecture (revised)\n20: - **Global** (unchanged): `config/tui-settings.json` in the manigot checkout\n21:   holds **personal** prefs — `editor`, `profile`. Gitignored, not shared.\n22: - **Project** (new): `docs/manigot.json` in the *target project* holds\n23:   **shared** project conventions — starting with `baseBranch`. Committable,\n24:   no secrets. Read by:\n25:   - the TUI (`m` shortcut, and the Settings form's base-branch field), via a\n26:     new Go package;\n27:   - `scripts/new-job.sh` directly (so the CLI `mg job \"...\"` respects it with\n28:     no Go→bash parameter passing — the script is the single reader at\n29:     job-creation time).\n30: \n31: This means `hostcmd.NewJob`'s signature does **not** change: the TUI still\n32: calls it as today, and `new-job.sh` reads `docs/manigot.json` for the base\n33: branch itself.\n34: \n35: ### Decisions applied (from human)\n36: 1. `finish-job.sh` / `delete-job.sh` **stay as-is** — they already auto-detect\n37:    via `git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` (fallback `main`); they are\n38:    not hardcoded. Out of scope.\n39: 2. Base branch is **project-scoped** (`docs/manigot.json`); CLI `mg job` reads\n40:    it too.\n41: 3. List-view hint becomes **\"m base branch\"**.\n42: \n43: ### Assumptions (confirm if wrong)\n44: - `editor` and `profile` remain **global/personal** (my editor, my\n45:   subscription); only `baseBranch` moves to the project file.\n46: - `docs/manigot.json` is meant to be **committed** by the target project\n47:   (shared team convention; contains only a public ref name, no secrets).\n48: \n49: ### Remaining decisions (analyst recommendation in brackets)\n50: - **File name/location**: `docs/manigot.json`. [`docs/manigot.json` — clearly\n51:   manigot-owned, lives beside `docs/AGENTS.md`, reachable by the existing\n52:   project-root walk-up on both sides.]\n53: - **Format**: JSON. [JSON, for consistency with `tui-settings.json` and clean\n54:   Go I/O. Bash reads the single `baseBranch` key via a guarded `sed`\n55:   extraction; revisit (add `jq`) only if more project keys appear.]\n56: - **Go package**: new `tui/internal/project` with `Settings`/`Load`/`Save`/\n57:   `Path`. [New package — distinct lifecycle/storage/sharing model from the\n58:   global `config` package. Alternative: extend `config`.]\n59: - **Seeding**: seed `project-template/docs/manigot.json` (default\n60:   `{\"baseBranch\":\"main\"}`) and copy it in `init.sh`. [Recommended — makes the\n61:   feature discoverable and committable from day one. Existing projects get it\n62:   created on first TUI save.]\n63: - **`--base-branch` override on `new-job.sh`**: keep as an optional override\n64:   flag. [Recommended — cheap, useful for ad-hoc one-offs.]\n65: \n66: ## Task breakdown\n67: \n68: TASK-1: Add a project-scoped settings package: `Settings{BaseBranch string}`\n69: (json `baseBranch,omitempty`), `Path(root)` → `<root>/docs/manigot.json`,\n70: `Load(root)` (missing/unreadable file ⇒ zero value, never an error, mirroring\n71: `config.Load`), `Save(root, s)` (writes JSON, `docs/` already exists in any\n72: initialized project), and `BaseBranchValue()` returning `\"main\"` when empty.\n73: Include a round-trip test + a default-when-empty test.\n74: files: tui/internal/project/settings.go (new), tui/internal/project/settings_test.go (new)\n75: depends: none\n76: risk: low — new, isolated package; pure additive I/O mirroring the proven\n77: `config` package shape.\n78: \n79: TASK-2: Add a base-branch text input to the Settings form and generalize the\n80: tab/shift+tab focus cycle from its current 2-field toggle (editor ↔ profile)\n81: to a 3-field cycle (editor → base branch → profile). The base-branch field\n82: reads/writes the **project** file, while editor+profile keep reading/writing\n83: the **global** file: `settingsView` carries both a global `config.Settings`\n84: and a project base-branch value; `settingsValue()` returns the global slice\n85: and a new `projectValue()` returns `project.Settings{BaseBranch}`. Label the\n86: base-branch row so it's clear it's project-scoped. Update the focus/render\n87: tests (they encode today's 2-field model) and add a `projectValue` test.\n88: files: tui/internal/ui/settings.go, tui/internal/ui/settings_test.go\n89: depends: TASK-1\n90: risk: medium — the tab/focus logic is a small but touchy refactor; four\n91: existing tests (TabTogglesFocus, ShiftTabTogglesFocusBackward,\n92: ProfileCycleOnlyWhenProfileFocused, Render) encode the 2-field assumption.\n93: \n94: TASK-3: Wire the project settings into the App: add a `projectSettings`\n95: field on `App`, load it (`project.Load(a.root)`) at startup, and on the\n96: settings form's submit call **both** `config.Save(global)` and\n97: `project.Save(a.root, projectVal)` (surface either error in the form's\n98: status). Pass the loaded project base branch into `newSettingsView`.\n99: files: tui/internal/ui/app.go (App struct, startup Load near line 132,\n100: updateSettings stSubmit around line 673, newSettingsView call around 639)\n101: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n102: risk: low-medium — straightforward wiring; the dual-save needs both errors\n103: handled; verify existing settings save still works.\n104: \n105: TASK-4: Make the list-view `m` quick-checkout use the configured base branch\n106: (`a.projectSettings.BaseBranchValue()`) instead of the literal `\"main\"`; change\n107: the footer hint at line 1220 from \"m main\" to **\"m base branch\"**; refresh\n108: `a.projectSettings` on the ctrl+r refresh path (so externally-edited\n109: `docs/manigot.json` is picked up); update the \"back to main\" comments\n110: (lines 316, 652–660) to be base-branch-neutral. Confirm the `m`-key tests in\n111: checkout_test.go still pass (default settings ⇒ `BaseBranchValue()` ⇒\n112: `\"main\"`, so assertions unchanged unless we add a non-default case).\n113: files: tui/internal/ui/app.go\n114: depends: TASK-1, TASK-3\n115: risk: low — single call-site change; default behavior preserved; well-covered\n116: by checkout_test.go.\n117: \n118: TASK-5: Teach `scripts/new-job.sh` to read the base branch from\n119: `docs/manigot.json` (guarded single-key `sed` extraction; default `\"main\"` when\n120: the file/key is absent), replace the `BASE_BRANCH=\"main\"` literal at line 70,\n121: add an optional `--base-branch <name>` override to the arg-parse loop, and\n122: update the usage block + `Usage:` error line. Validate the resolved base\n123: branch exists as a local ref (the existing check at lines 74–77 already does).\n124: files: scripts/new-job.sh\n125: depends: TASK-1 (agrees the JSON shape the bash extractor targets)\n126: risk: low — isolated script edit; default preserves current behavior. The\n127: bash JSON extraction is the one fragile spot (single known key, regex-bounded);\n128: note in a code comment that adding more project keys warrants `jq`.\n129: \n130: TASK-6: Seed the project settings file in the template/init flow and sync all\n131: documentation (hard rule: AGENTS.md / project-template stay in sync):\n132: - add `project-template/docs/manigot.json` with `{\"baseBranch\":\"main\"}`;\n133: - add a `cp` line + echo to `scripts/init.sh` (fresh projects get it; existing\n134:   projects get it created on first TUI save);\n135: - in `docs/AGENTS.md` **and** `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md`: document\n136:   `docs/manigot.json` as the new project settings file; update the\n137:   `scripts/new-job.sh` description (\"branched from main\" → from the configured\n138:   base branch); update the `mg job` command line; clarify in the\n139:   `config/tui-settings.json` bullet that it holds personal prefs (editor/\n140:   profile) and that base branch now lives in the project file;\n141: - verify `agents/*.md` need no change (earlier grep showed only comments/test\n142:   fixtures referencing \"main\", nothing functional).\n143: files: project-template/docs/manigot.json (new), scripts/init.sh,\n144: docs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md\n145: depends: TASK-1 … TASK-5 (so docs describe the final behavior)\n146: risk: low — documentation + template seeding; mechanical edits.\n147: \n148: ## Suggested order\n149: TASK-1 → TASK-2 + TASK-5 (parallel) → TASK-3 → TASK-4 → TASK-6.\n150: Build with `make tui && make jdi`; run `go test ./...` from `tui/`.\n151: \n152: ## Notes for the developer\n153: - No change to `hostcmd.NewJob` or its tests, and no change to `updateNewJob`'s\n154:   call site: `new-job.sh` reads `docs/manigot.json` itself, so the TUI keeps\n155:   invoking job creation exactly as today.\n156: - `finish-job.sh` / `delete-job.sh` are intentionally untouched (decision #1).\n157: - The project file is committable (no secrets); do not add it to any gitignore.\n158: - If `docs/` is absent (TUI baseline is that it exists, since jobs live in\n159:   `docs/jobs/`), `project.Load` returns the zero value ⇒ `\"main\"`, and\n160:   `project.Save` would simply fail and surface in the form status.\n\n(End of file - total 160 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: Set default branch in settings\n\nid: 6kbt43\nstatus: open\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-08-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md, revised after human decisions. -->\n\n## Scope summary\n\nMake the base branch (hardcoded as `main`) user-configurable, defaulting to\n`main`, so projects on `develop`/`master`/`trunk` can use the TUI. Per human\ndecision #2, the base branch lives in a **project-scoped settings file**\n(`docs/manigot.json`), not the global TUI settings — base branch is a shared\nproject convention, so it travels with the project (committable) and is read\nby both the TUI and the bare CLI `mg job`.\n\n### Architecture (revised)\n- **Global** (unchanged): `config/tui-settings.json` in the manigot checkout","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/6kbt43_set-default-branch-in-settings/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: Set default branch in settings\n\nid: 6kbt43\nstatus: open\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-08-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md, revised after human decisions. -->\n\n## Scope summary\n\nMake the base branch (hardcoded as `main`) user-configurable, defaulting to\n`main`, so projects on `develop`/`master`/`trunk` can use the TUI. Per human\ndecision #2, the base branch lives in a **project-scoped settings file**\n(`docs/manigot.json`), not the global TUI settings — base branch is a shared\nproject convention, so it travels with the project (committable) and is read\nby both the TUI and the bare CLI `mg job`.\n\n### Architecture (revised)\n- **Global** (unchanged): `config/tui-settings.json` in the manigot checkout\n  holds **personal** prefs — `editor`, `profile`. Gitignored, not shared.\n- **Project** (new): `docs/manigot.json` in the *target project* holds\n  **shared** project conventions — starting with `baseBranch`. Committable,\n  no secrets. Read by:\n  - the TUI (`m` shortcut, and the Settings form's base-branch field), via a\n    new Go package;\n  - `scripts/new-job.sh` directly (so the CLI `mg job \"...\"` respects it with\n    no Go→bash parameter passing — the script is the single reader at\n    job-creation time).\n\nThis means `hostcmd.NewJob`'s signature does **not** change: the TUI still\ncalls it as today, and `new-job.sh` reads `docs/manigot.json` for the base\nbranch itself.\n\n### Decisions applied (from human)\n1. `finish-job.sh` / `delete-job.sh` **stay as-is** — they already auto-detect\n   via `git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` (fallback `main`); they are\n   not hardcoded. Out of scope.\n2. Base branch is **project-scoped** (`docs/manigot.json`); CLI `mg job` reads\n   it too.\n3. List-view hint becomes **\"m base branch\"**.\n\n### Assumptions (confirm if wrong)\n- `editor` and `profile` remain **global/personal** (my editor, my\n  subscription); only `baseBranch` moves to the project file.\n- `docs/manigot.json` is meant to be **committed** by the target project\n  (shared team convention; contains only a public ref name, no secrets).\n\n### Remaining decisions (analyst recommendation in brackets)\n- **File name/location**: `docs/manigot.json`. [`docs/manigot.json` — clearly\n  manigot-owned, lives beside `docs/AGENTS.md`, reachable by the existing\n  project-root walk-up on both sides.]\n- **Format**: JSON. [JSON, for consistency with `tui-settings.json` and clean\n  Go I/O. Bash reads the single `baseBranch` key via a guarded `sed`\n  extraction; revisit (add `jq`) only if more project keys appear.]\n- **Go package**: new `tui/internal/project` with `Settings`/`Load`/`Save`/\n  `Path`. [New package — distinct lifecycle/storage/sharing model from the\n  global `config` package. Alternative: extend `config`.]\n- **Seeding**: seed `project-template/docs/manigot.json` (default\n  `{\"baseBranch\":\"main\"}`) and copy it in `init.sh`. [Recommended — makes the\n  feature discoverable and committable from day one. Existing projects get it\n  created on first TUI save.]\n- **`--base-branch` override on `new-job.sh`**: keep as an optional override\n  flag. [Recommended — cheap, useful for ad-hoc one-offs.]\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Add a project-scoped settings package: `Settings{BaseBranch string}`\n(json `baseBranch,omitempty`), `Path(root)` → `<root>/docs/manigot.json`,\n`Load(root)` (missing/unreadable file ⇒ zero value, never an error, mirroring\n`config.Load`), `Save(root, s)` (writes JSON, `docs/` already exists in any\ninitialized project), and `BaseBranchValue()` returning `\"main\"` when empty.\nInclude a round-trip test + a default-when-empty test.\nfiles: tui/internal/project/settings.go (new), tui/internal/project/settings_test.go (new)\ndepends: none\nrisk: low — new, isolated package; pure additive I/O mirroring the proven\n`config` package shape.\n\nTASK-2: Add a base-branch text input to the Settings form and generalize the\ntab/shift+tab focus cycle from its current 2-field toggle (editor ↔ profile)\nto a 3-field cycle (editor → base branch → profile). The base-branch field\nreads/writes the **project** file, while editor+profile keep reading/writing\nthe **global** file: `settingsView` carries both a global `config.Settings`\nand a project base-branch value; `settingsValue()` returns the global slice\nand a new `projectValue()` returns `project.Settings{BaseBranch}`. Label the\nbase-branch row so it's clear it's project-scoped. Update the focus/render\ntests (they encode today's 2-field model) and add a `projectValue` test.\nfiles: tui/internal/ui/settings.go, tui/internal/ui/settings_test.go\ndepends: TASK-1\nrisk: medium — the tab/focus logic is a small but touchy refactor; four\nexisting tests (TabTogglesFocus, ShiftTabTogglesFocusBackward,\nProfileCycleOnlyWhenProfileFocused, Render) encode the 2-field assumption.\n\nTASK-3: Wire the project settings into the App: add a `projectSettings`\nfield on `App`, load it (`project.Load(a.root)`) at startup, and on the\nsettings form's submit call **both** `config.Save(global)` and\n`project.Save(a.root, projectVal)` (surface either error in the form's\nstatus). Pass the loaded project base branch into `newSettingsView`.\nfiles: tui/internal/ui/app.go (App struct, startup Load near line 132,\nupdateSettings stSubmit around line 673, newSettingsView call around 639)\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2\nrisk: low-medium — straightforward wiring; the dual-save needs both errors\nhandled; verify existing settings save still works.\n\nTASK-4: Make the list-view `m` quick-checkout use the configured base branch\n(`a.projectSettings.BaseBranchValue()`) instead of the literal `\"main\"`; change\nthe footer hint at line 1220 from \"m main\" to **\"m base branch\"**; refresh\n`a.projectSettings` on the ctrl+r refresh path (so externally-edited\n`docs/manigot.json` is picked up); update the \"back to main\" comments\n(lines 316, 652–660) to be base-branch-neutral. Confirm the `m`-key tests in\ncheckout_test.go still pass (default settings ⇒ `BaseBranchValue()` ⇒\n`\"main\"`, so assertions unchanged unless we add a non-default case).\nfiles: tui/internal/ui/app.go\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-3\nrisk: low — single call-site change; default behavior preserved; well-covered\nby checkout_test.go.\n\nTASK-5: Teach `scripts/new-job.sh` to read the base branch from\n`docs/manigot.json` (guarded single-key `sed` extraction; default `\"main\"` when\nthe file/key is absent), replace the `BASE_BRANCH=\"main\"` literal at line 70,\nadd an optional `--base-branch <name>` override to the arg-parse loop, and\nupdate the usage block + `Usage:` error line. Validate the resolved base\nbranch exists as a local ref (the existing check at lines 74–77 already does).\nfiles: scripts/new-job.sh\ndepends: TASK-1 (agrees the JSON shape the bash extractor targets)\nrisk: low — isolated script edit; default preserves current behavior. The\nbash JSON extraction is the one fragile spot (single known key, regex-bounded);\nnote in a code comment that adding more project keys warrants `jq`.\n\nTASK-6: Seed the project settings file in the template/init flow and sync all\ndocumentation (hard rule: AGENTS.md / project-template stay in sync):\n- add `project-template/docs/manigot.json` with `{\"baseBranch\":\"main\"}`;\n- add a `cp` line + echo to `scripts/init.sh` (fresh projects get it; existing\n  projects get it created on first TUI save);\n- in `docs/AGENTS.md` **and** `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md`: document\n  `docs/manigot.json` as the new project settings file; update the\n  `scripts/new-job.sh` description (\"branched from main\" → from the configured\n  base branch); update the `mg job` command line; clarify in the\n  `config/tui-settings.json` bullet that it holds personal prefs (editor/\n  profile) and that base branch now lives in the project file;\n- verify `agents/*.md` need no change (earlier grep showed only comments/test\n  fixtures referencing \"main\", nothing functional).\nfiles: project-template/docs/manigot.json (new), scripts/init.sh,\ndocs/AGENTS.md, project-template/docs/AGENTS.md\ndepends: TASK-1 … TASK-5 (so docs describe the final behavior)\nrisk: low — documentation + template seeding; mechanical edits.\n\n## Suggested order\nTASK-1 → TASK-2 + TASK-5 (parallel) → TASK-3 → TASK-4 → TASK-6.\nBuild with `make tui && make jdi`; run `go test ./...` from `tui/`.\n\n## Notes for the developer\n- No change to `hostcmd.NewJob` or its tests, and no change to `updateNewJob`'s\n  call site: `new-job.sh` reads `docs/manigot.json` itself, so the TUI keeps\n  invoking job creation exactly as today.\n- `finish-job.sh` / `delete-job.sh` are intentionally untouched (decision #1).\n- The project file is committable (no secrets); do not add it to any gitignore.\n- If `docs/` is absent (TUI baseline is that it exists, since jobs live in\n  `docs/jobs/`), `project.Load` returns the zero value ⇒ `\"main\"`, and\n  `project.Save` would simply fail and surface in the form status.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":160,"totalLines":160,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/6kbt43_set-default-branch-in-settings/tasks.md","time":{"start":1787919338982,"end":1787919338986}},"id":"prt_0484c0cf9001O8EikNGNzoBOiy","sessionID":"ses_fb7b4a8d5ffeJWKjfWHud2qnLO","messageID":"msg_0484c0549001Lwb2PYazs0CWZp"}}
