{"type":"text","timestamp":1787919639165,"sessionID":"ses_fb7b4a8d5ffeJWKjfWHud2qnLO","part":{"id":"prt_0485080f8001EaMd9Ug5HlFv3V","messageID":"msg_048506fbb0016M7weVsyxWjlld","sessionID":"ses_fb7b4a8d5ffeJWKjfWHud2qnLO","type":"text","text":"I've analyzed the job and written the analyst deliverable to `tasks.md`. Here is the structured task list.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n**TASK-1: Restructure the settings form render into two bold-headed sections with per-setting bold headlines and de-emphasized examples.**\n- **Files:** `src/internal/ui/settings.go` (render + doc comment; possibly a new style in `src/internal/ui/styles.go`)\n- **Dependencies:** none\n- **Risk:** medium — the render is pinned by existing tests that TASK-2 must update in lockstep; the form is *not scrollable* and already sits at ~30 lines, so the two new section headlines must be paid for by cutting blank lines and shortening examples or the footer gets cut off at 24 rows; dim-only-the-value focus logic is a small behavior change.\n\n**TASK-2: Update `settings_test.go` for the new layout and extend coverage of the new structure (section headlines, shortened examples, profile rows).**\n- **Files:** `src/internal/ui/settings_test.go`\n- **Dependencies:** TASK-1 (asserts its actual output strings)\n- **Risk:** low — test-only, but must land in the same commit as TASK-1 or the suite goes red; assertion strings must be written from the implemented output, not from the proposal sketch.\n\n## Key analysis notes\n\n- **Branch verified:** the workspace's `.git` points at `worktrees/extension_settings-layout`, matching the brief's `branch: fix/extension_settings-layout` — this is the job's own worktree.\n- **Scope is render-only:** the settings view (`settingsView.render()` in `src/internal/ui/settings.go`) is a plain, non-scrollable string; all persistence, focus-cycle, and tab-order logic must stay byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **The redesign's three goals** (from the brief): separation (two sections — Personal vs Project, matching the storage split the code already documents), bold headlines per setting, and examples made less visually present (shortened, single persistence note per section instead of per field).\n- **Height is the binding constraint:** the form is rendered raw with no viewport, so the redesign must not grow the line count — the profile block's two dim description lines are flagged as the first trim candidate if needed.\n- **No render report exists** for this job, so the developer must verify fitted height manually in a real `mg tui` session (noted in the tasks file).\n\nThe brief's scope was clear enough that no human decision was required; the \"think about improvements yourself\" instruction was answered with a concrete proposal in the scope summary, while leaving implementation detail to the developer.","time":{"start":1787919630584,"end":1787919639163}}}
