{"type":"text","timestamp":1787920557883,"sessionID":"ses_fb7af5935ffeLyhZ1lIHw0GPEP","part":{"id":"prt_0485e923e001WEwT3pKV3G1FT2","messageID":"msg_0485e8cb5001yM1Vw0RKyfH5eQ","sessionID":"ses_fb7af5935ffeLyhZ1lIHw0GPEP","type":"text","text":"Both tasks are complete and committed. Summary of the work:\n\n## What was done\n\n**TASK-1 — Restructured the settings form render** (`src/internal/ui/settings.go`):\n- Split the seven settings into two bold-headed sections matching the storage split: **Personal settings** (editor, recent activity, profile, terminal, theme) and **Project settings** (base branch, job branch prefix).\n- Each section headline carries the storage location once as a dim suffix, so the per-field \"stored in …\" clauses could be dropped (the \"(project)\" label suffixes went away too).\n- Bold headline per setting (`headerStyle`) with the value next to it in a fixed aligned label column (new `settingsLabelWidth` const + `settingsField` helper); only the input value dims when unfocused, never the bold headline.\n- Examples shortened and de-emphasized (dim, 2-space indent); removed the redundant \"tool: … · billed via …\" selected-profile description line.\n- Vertical noise reduced — blanks kept only around the profile block, between sections, and before the footer. The form shrinks from **30 → 28 lines**.\n- All interaction semantics preserved byte-for-byte: tab cycle order, profile ←/→ cycling, enter/esc, focus-aware footer hint.\n\n**TASK-2 — Updated/extended tests** (`src/internal/ui/settings_test.go`):\n- `TestSettingsRender` rewritten for the new strings, plus assertions that the old phrasing is gone.\n- New tests: `TestSettingsRenderPersistenceNotesOncePerSection` (each storage note appears exactly once) and `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget` (pins 23 + per-profile lines, guarding the height budget).\n\n**Verification**: module builds clean; all 25 settings/new-job tests pass. The ~53 other ui-package failures are pre-existing environment restrictions (the session's git shim refuses `git init` in temp repos, and tig isn't installed) — unrelated to this change.\n\n**Known limitation** (recorded in `implementation.md`): the form still renders 28 lines, so in a 24-row terminal the Project settings section and footer remain cut off (content area is 22 rows after padding) — but that was already true of the old 30-line layout, and this is 2 lines closer to fitting.\n\nBoth commits are on `fix/extension_settings-layout`; the worktree is clean.","time":{"start":1787920552510,"end":1787920557881}}}
