d":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md","time":{"start":1787920661275,"end":1787920661279}},"id":"prt_048603a46001CrAIqu41B7Fz3E","sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","messageID":"msg_048600bff001ow22Ek0cTcR3x8"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787920661337,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","part":{"id":"prt_0486010c4001MrVqA3m40ThGfX","messageID":"msg_048600bff001ow22Ek0cTcR3x8","sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","type":"text","text":"At a 24-row terminal: `a.height = 24 - 2*1 = 22`. So the settings form is rendered at height 22, and `uiPaddingStyle` adds back 1 top + 1 bottom = 24 rows total. The 28-line form overflows the 22-row content area. Confirmed.\n\nSo at a standard 80×24 terminal, the settings form's last 6 lines (the entire Project settings section: \"Project settings\" headline, Base branch field+example, Job branch prefix field+example, and the footer hint) are all below the visible area — silently cut off.\n\nThis is a real functional problem for the layout-improvement job: two of the seven settings (Base branch, Job branch prefix) are entirely unreachable/visible at the standard terminal size, and the save/cancel footer hint is invisible.\n\nLet me also confirm whether the settingsView.resize does anything to the content. Let me quickly check resize for settingsView - it likely just stores width/height.\n\nLet me check the newSettingsView and resize.\n\nActually, I've confirmed the key facts. The render is a raw fixed-height string regardless of the height param (the render doesn't use v.height at all — it's a fixed 28-line string). So height is irrelevant; the form is 28 lines always, overflowing 22 content rows.\n\nLet me confirm render doesn't use height.\n\nFrom the render code I read, it's all fixed lines, no v.height usage. Confirmed.\n\nNow let me finalize. I'll write the verdict.\n\nGiven the explicit task requirement about the 24-row fit and the footer being visible, plus the Project settings section being fully cut off at a standard terminal size, I'll mark this NEEDS WORK.\n\nLet me reconsider one more time if this is too harsh. The counterpoint: the analyst's own sketch was 32 lines, meaning even the analyst's proposed design wouldn't fit. And the developer improved to 28. But the task explicitly and repeatedly emphasized the height budget and required verification of footer visibility. The developer's own \"known issues\" admits it's cut off. For a layout job whose entire purpose is readability, having 2 of 7 settings + the footer completely invisible at a standard 80×24 terminal is a meaningful gap against the stated requirement.\n\nI'll render NEEDS WORK with the height as the single blocker. This is a layout job; the off-screen Project settings section is functionally important. I'll be specific and constructive.\n\nLet me also double-check TASK-2's tests don't have errors. The test asserts `23 + len(profileOptions)` = 28 lines. My manual count matches 28. The persistence notes test: \"saved in config/tui-settings.json + manigot/.env\" appears once (in Personal settings headline) — yes once. \"stored in .manigot/manigot.json, shared with your team\" once (Project settings headline). \"saved as MANIGOT_PROFILE in manigot/.env\" once (profile note). Good.\n\nThe `gone` assertions: \"Editor:\" — the new render uses \"Editor\" without colon in settingsField. Correct, no colon. \"stored in config/tui-settings.json\" — not present. \"saved as OPENCODE_THEME\" — not present (theme example is \"blank = OpenCode's own default · OpenCode only\"). \"max entries shown in the\" — not present. \"billed via\" — removed. Good.\n\nNow let me write the verdict.\n\nLet me check the current verdict.md to see if it already exists and its state.\n\n","time":{"start":1787920650436,"end":1787920661335}}}
