{"type":"text","timestamp":1787920692574,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","part":{"id":"prt_048604059001NvC4hOzdTMxqZB","messageID":"msg_048603b63001xZlXaInDCOQX9D","sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","type":"text","text":"The session.log is modified (uncommitted leftover from the session — this will be swept). Now let me write the verdict.\n\nLet me reconsider the severity of the height issue one final time to make a fair, well-calibrated judgment.\n\nThe task explicitly stated (developer notes, line 160-166):\n> The form is not scrollable and already sits at the edge of a 24-row terminal — after implementing, run `mg tui`, open settings (`s`), and check at 24 rows and at a narrow width that the footer (\"enter save · esc cancel\") is still visible and nothing important is cut off.\n\nThis is an explicit requirement. The implementation:\n- Reduced 30 → 28 lines (improvement)\n- But 28 lines still exceeds the 22 content rows available at 24-row terminal (after 1 top + 1 bottom padding)\n- The **entire Project settings section** (Base branch, Job branch prefix — 2 of the 7 settings) and the footer are cut off\n- The developer acknowledged this in Known issues but did not resolve it or escalate\n\nFor a job whose entire purpose is improving settings layout readability, having the Project settings section completely off-screen at the standard 80×24 terminal size is a significant functional gap against the explicitly stated requirement. The `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget` test is also misnamed — it asserts 23+len(profileOptions)=28 lines (a regression guard relative to the old ~30), but does NOT assert the actual 24-row/22-content-row budget that the task required.\n\nI'll render NEEDS WORK with this as the blocker.\n\n","time":{"start":1787920662617,"end":1787920692573}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787920692587,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-90b96afdb7534543","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md","content":"# Verdict: settings layout\n\nid: extension\nstatus: open\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nTASK-1: PARTIAL\nnotes: The render restructure is well executed and meets the three design goals\n(section separation, bold per-setting headlines with the value next to them,\nde-emphasized examples, dim-only-the-value focus). `settingsField` +\n`settingsLabelWidth` align the inputs cleanly, the persistence-location note\nmoves to the section headlines once, and interaction semantics are preserved\n(focus-cycle order, profile cycling, enter/esc, `hint()` footer). However, the\n**height budget requirement is not met.** The task explicitly required\n(`tasks.md` notes, \"Height constraint\"): *\"check at 24 rows ... that the footer\n('enter save · esc cancel') is still visible and nothing important is cut off.\"*\n\nAt a standard 80×24 terminal the content area is only 22 rows\n(`app.go` `View()` wraps in `uiPaddingStyle` 1-top + 1-bottom;\n`WindowSizeMsg` sets `a.height = msg.Height - 2*uiPaddingY` = 22). The new\nrender is a fixed 28-line string (`settings.go` `render()`), so 6 lines fall\nbelow the visible area: the **entire Project settings section** (\"Project\nsettings\" headline, Base branch field + example, Job branch prefix field +\nexample) **and the footer hint are cut off.** Two of the seven settings are\ntherefore invisible/unreachable at the standard terminal size, and the\nsave/cancel hint is gone. The developer's own `implementation.md` Known issues\nconfirms the cut-off and treats it as out of scope; but this was an explicit,\nrepeatedly-emphasized task requirement, not optional. For a layout-improvement\njob, off-screen settings are a functional gap, not just a cosmetic nit.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `settings_test.go` is updated correctly and matches the implemented\nrender (section headlines, per-setting labels, typed value, profile rows,\nshortened examples, and the `gone` assertions for removed phrasing).\n`TestSettingsRenderPersistenceNotesOncePerSection` correctly asserts each\npersistence note appears exactly once. Model-level tests (focus cycle,\nshift+tab, profile cycling, edit/seeding) are untouched and remain valid since\nthey operate on the model, not the render. One caveat: `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget`\nis misnamed — it pins the line count at `23 + len(profileOptions)` = 28 as a\nregression guard against the old ~30, but it does **not** assert the actual\n24-row / 22-content-row budget the task required. It therefore passes while the\nreal height requirement fails. This should be fixed to assert the true budget\n(or the form compressed so it actually fits).\n\n## Security\n\nnone (render-only change; no filesystem, credential, or network surface touched).\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nBlockers before merge:\n1. The 24-row height budget must be met. At a standard 80×24 terminal the\n   Project settings section (Base branch, Job branch prefix — 2 of the 7\n   settings) and the footer are fully cut off, which the task explicitly\n   required to be visible. Either compress the render to fit the 22 content\n   rows (drop blank lines, merge/shorten the profile note and example lines,\n   tighten section separation — the analyst's own guidance prioritized these\n   over section separation) or otherwise resolve the overflow. The developer\n   should verify in a real `mg tui` at 24 rows and confirm the footer and\n   Project settings are visible.\n2. `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget` should assert the real budget (that the\n   render fits the 22 content rows available at a 24-row terminal), not merely\n   a fixed 28-line count, so the height requirement is actually guarded by a\n   test.\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md","time":{"start":1787920692571,"end":1787920692578}},"id":"prt_0486050c0001o4VHmee8FvNtDS","sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","messageID":"msg_048603b63001xZlXaInDCOQX9D"}}
