{"type":"text","timestamp":1787920703368,"sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","part":{"id":"prt_04860c6b8001LkfZc4BpW1RtXk","messageID":"msg_04860c3a2001ActCXBEWE32Ypj","sessionID":"ses_fb7a153fcffeJhFRBIm7QrxDfI","type":"text","text":"I've completed the review and written the verdict.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Verdict: NEEDS WORK**\n\n**TASK-1 (render restructure): PARTIAL.** The three design goals from the brief are well executed — two bold section headlines, a bold headline per setting with the value next to it (aligned via `settingsField` + `settingsLabelWidth`), de-emphasized examples, and dim-only-the-value focus. Interaction semantics are preserved. **However, the height budget requirement is not met.** The task explicitly required that at 24 rows the footer be visible and nothing important cut off. At a standard 80×24 terminal the content area is only 22 rows (after `uiPaddingStyle`'s 1-top/1-bottom padding), but the form renders a fixed 28 lines — so the **entire Project settings section** (Base branch, Job branch prefix — 2 of the 7 settings) **and the footer are silently cut off.** The developer acknowledged this in Known issues and treated it as out of scope, but it was an explicit, repeatedly-emphasized task requirement, and off-screen settings are a functional gap for a layout job.\n\n**TASK-2 (tests): PASS** for correctness of the updates, but `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget` is misnamed — it only pins the line count at 28 rather than asserting the real 22-content-row budget, so it passes while the actual height requirement fails.\n\nThe two blockers are: (1) make the form fit 22 content rows at a 24-row terminal (footer + Project settings visible), and (2) make the height-budget test assert the real budget.","time":{"start":1787920697016,"end":1787920703365}}}
