{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787920739481,"sessionID":"ses_fb79f1c04ffeYG6ohZOnXBocr5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_2oj4Gle9eVNpJEx57svd9899","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/src/internal/ui/app.go","offset":540,"limit":75},"output":"<path>/workspace/src/internal/ui/app.go</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n540: \t\t// reads (job list, project settings, open detail view, git-log strip)\n541: \t\t// so a TUI left sitting in a tmux pane catches up on its own — the\n542: \t\t// brief's \"came back to the TUI and want to see what happened\"\n543: \t\t// outcome, with the jdi stop-bell (pollJDIBell, via refreshJobs)\n544: \t\t// riding along for free. Deliberately silent: no status line, unlike\n545: \t\t// ctrl+r's \"refreshed · N job(s)\" — a footer status every second\n546: \t\t// would blink constantly and drown out real feedback.\n547: \t\t//\n548: \t\t// State gating: refresh() is skipped in the form/overlay states\n549: \t\t// (stateNewJob, stateSettings, stateAgents, stateConfirm,\n550: \t\t// stateGitPanel), where reloading the list or the detail view under\n551: \t\t// an open form/picker/confirmation would be disruptive; the chain\n552: \t\t// itself keeps ticking regardless, so a single chain lives for the\n553: \t\t// app's lifetime. The spinner cmd refresh produced is propagated the\n554: \t\t// way ctrl+r propagates it (a tick is a discovery point for runs\n555: \t\t// started outside this session), and the chain always re-arms.\n556: \t\tswitch a.state {\n557: \t\tcase stateList, stateDetail:\n558: \t\t\tspinnerCmd := a.refresh()\n559: \t\t\treturn a, tea.Batch(spinnerCmd, a.autoRefreshCmd())\n560: \t\tdefault:\n561: \t\t\treturn a, a.autoRefreshCmd()\n562: \t\t}\n563: \tcase tea.KeyMsg:\n564: \t\t// Global keys handled in every state.\n565: \t\tswitch msg.String() {\n566: \t\tcase \"ctrl+c\":\n567: \t\t\treturn a, tea.Quit\n568: \t\t}\n569: \t\tswitch a.state {\n570: \t\tcase stateList:\n571: \t\t\treturn a.updateList(msg)\n572: \t\tcase stateDetail:\n573: \t\t\treturn a.updateDetail(msg)\n574: \t\tcase stateNewJob:\n575: \t\t\treturn a.updateNewJob(msg)\n576: \t\tcase stateSettings:\n577: \t\t\treturn a.updateSettings(msg)\n578: \t\tcase stateAgents:\n579: \t\t\treturn a.updateAgentsPicker(msg)\n580: \t\tcase stateConfirm:\n581: \t\t\treturn a.updateConfirm(msg)\n582: \t\tcase stateGitPanel:\n583: \t\t\treturn a.updateGitPanel(msg)\n584: \t\t}\n585: \t}\n586: \treturn a, nil\n587: }\n588: \n589: // View renders the active view, padded out to the terminal edge — see\n590: // uiPaddingStyle.\n591: func (a *App) View() string {\n592: \tvar content string\n593: \tswitch a.state {\n594: \tcase stateDetail:\n595: \t\tcontent = a.detail.render()\n596: \tcase stateNewJob:\n597: \t\tcontent = a.newJob.render()\n598: \tcase stateSettings:\n599: \t\tcontent = a.settingsView.render()\n600: \tcase stateAgents:\n601: \t\tcontent = a.agentsPicker.render()\n602: \tcase stateConfirm:\n603: \t\tcontent = a.confirm.render()\n604: \tcase stateGitPanel:\n605: \t\tcontent = a.gitPanelOverlay()\n606: \tdefault:\n607: \t\tcontent = a.list.render(a.jobs, a.status, a.statusVisible(), a.settings.RecentActivityCountValue(), a.spinnerStep, a.width, a.height)\n608: \t}\n609: \treturn uiPaddingStyle.Render(content)\n610: }\n611: \n612: // refreshRecentCommits re-reads the recent-activity strip from git, always\n613: // fetching up to the configured maximum (Settings.RecentActivityCountValue).\n614: // How many of those cached commits actually get rendered is decided later, at\n\n(Showing lines 540-614 of 1662. Use offset=615 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\t\t// reads (job list, project settings, open detail view, git-log strip)\n\t\t// so a TUI left sitting in a tmux pane catches up on its own — the\n\t\t// brief's \"came back to the TUI and want to see what happened\"\n\t\t// outcome, with the jdi stop-bell (pollJDIBell, via refreshJobs)\n\t\t// riding along for fr