{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787920810629,"sessionID":"ses_fb79f1c04ffeYG6ohZOnXBocr5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a1c1d4237f19f8df","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Verdict: settings layout\n2: \n3: id: extension\n4: status: open\n5: reviewer: @reviewer\n6: date: 2026-08-28\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Review\n11: \n12: TASK-1: PARTIAL\n13: notes: The render restructure is well executed and meets the three design goals\n14: (section separation, bold per-setting headlines with the value next to them,\n15: de-emphasized examples, dim-only-the-value focus). `settingsField` +\n16: `settingsLabelWidth` align the inputs cleanly, the persistence-location note\n17: moves to the section headlines once, and interaction semantics are preserved\n18: (focus-cycle order, profile cycling, enter/esc, `hint()` footer). However, the\n19: **height budget requirement is not met.** The task explicitly required\n20: (`tasks.md` notes, \"Height constraint\"): *\"check at 24 rows ... that the footer\n21: ('enter save · esc cancel') is still visible and nothing important is cut off.\"*\n22: \n23: At a standard 80×24 terminal the content area is only 22 rows\n24: (`app.go` `View()` wraps in `uiPaddingStyle` 1-top + 1-bottom;\n25: `WindowSizeMsg` sets `a.height = msg.Height - 2*uiPaddingY` = 22). The new\n26: render is a fixed 28-line string (`settings.go` `render()`), so 6 lines fall\n27: below the visible area: the **entire Project settings section** (\"Project\n28: settings\" headline, Base branch field + example, Job branch prefix field +\n29: example) **and the footer hint are cut off.** Two of the seven settings are\n30: therefore invisible/unreachable at the standard terminal size, and the\n31: save/cancel hint is gone. The developer's own `implementation.md` Known issues\n32: confirms the cut-off and treats it as out of scope; but this was an explicit,\n33: repeatedly-emphasized task requirement, not optional. For a layout-improvement\n34: job, off-screen settings are a functional gap, not just a cosmetic nit.\n35: \n36: TASK-2: PASS\n37: notes: `settings_test.go` is updated correctly and matches the implemented\n38: render (section headlines, per-setting labels, typed value, profile rows,\n39: shortened examples, and the `gone` assertions for removed phrasing).\n40: `TestSettingsRenderPersistenceNotesOncePerSection` correctly asserts each\n41: persistence note appears exactly once. Model-level tests (focus cycle,\n42: shift+tab, profile cycling, edit/seeding) are untouched and remain valid since\n43: they operate on the model, not the render. One caveat: `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget`\n44: is misnamed — it pins the line count at `23 + len(profileOptions)` = 28 as a\n45: regression guard against the old ~30, but it does **not** assert the actual\n46: 24-row / 22-content-row budget the task required. It therefore passes while the\n47: real height requirement fails. This should be fixed to assert the true budget\n48: (or the form compressed so it actually fits).\n49: \n50: ## Security\n51: \n52: none (render-only change; no filesystem, credential, or network surface touched).\n53: \n54: ## Overall\n55: \n56: NEEDS WORK\n57: \n58: Blockers before merge:\n59: 1. The 24-row height budget must be met. At a standard 80×24 terminal the\n60:    Project settings section (Base branch, Job branch prefix — 2 of the 7\n61:    settings) and the footer are fully cut off, which the task explicitly\n62:    required to be visible. Either compress the render to fit the 22 content\n63:    rows (drop blank lines, merge/shorten the profile note and example lines,\n64:    tighten section separation — the analyst's own guidance prioritized these\n65:    over section separation) or otherwise resolve the overflow. The developer\n66:    should verify in a real `mg tui` at 24 rows and confirm the footer and\n67:    Project settings are visible.\n68: 2. `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget` should assert the real budget (that the\n69:    render fits the 22 content rows available at a 24-row terminal), not merely\n70:    a fixed 28-line count, so the height requirement is actually guarded by a\n71:    test.\n\n(End of file - total 71 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Verdict: settings layout\n\nid: extension\nstatus: open\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nTASK-1: PARTIAL\nnotes: The render restructure is well executed and meets the three design goals\n(section separation, bold per-setting headlines with the value next to them,\nde-emphasized examples, dim-only-the-value focus). `settingsField` +\n`settingsLabelWidth` align the inputs cleanly, the persistence-location note\nmoves to the section headlines once, and interaction semantics are preserved\n(focus-cycle order, profile cycling, enter/esc, `hint()` footer). However, the\n**height budget requirement is not met.** The task explicitly required\n(`tasks.md` notes, \"Height constraint\"): *\"check at 24 rows ... that the footer","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md","text":"# Verdict: settings layout\n\nid: extension\nstatus: open\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-08-28\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nTASK-1: PARTIAL\nnotes: The render restructure is well executed and meets the three design goals\n(section separation, bold per-setting headlines with the value next to them,\nde-emphasized examples, dim-only-the-value focus). `settingsField` +\n`settingsLabelWidth` align the inputs cleanly, the persistence-location note\nmoves to the section headlines once, and interaction semantics are preserved\n(focus-cycle order, profile cycling, enter/esc, `hint()` footer). However, the\n**height budget requirement is not met.** The task explicitly required\n(`tasks.md` notes, \"Height constraint\"): *\"check at 24 rows ... that the footer\n('enter save · esc cancel') is still visible and nothing important is cut off.\"*\n\nAt a standard 80×24 terminal the content area is only 22 rows\n(`app.go` `View()` wraps in `uiPaddingStyle` 1-top + 1-bottom;\n`WindowSizeMsg` sets `a.height = msg.Height - 2*uiPaddingY` = 22). The new\nrender is a fixed 28-line string (`settings.go` `render()`), so 6 lines fall\nbelow the visible area: the **entire Project settings section** (\"Project\nsettings\" headline, Base branch field + example, Job branch prefix field +\nexample) **and the footer hint are cut off.** Two of the seven settings are\ntherefore invisible/unreachable at the standard terminal size, and the\nsave/cancel hint is gone. The developer's own `implementation.md` Known issues\nconfirms the cut-off and treats it as out of scope; but this was an explicit,\nrepeatedly-emphasized task requirement, not optional. For a layout-improvement\njob, off-screen settings are a functional gap, not just a cosmetic nit.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `settings_test.go` is updated correctly and matches the implemented\nrender (section headlines, per-setting labels, typed value, profile rows,\nshortened examples, and the `gone` assertions for removed phrasing).\n`TestSettingsRenderPersistenceNotesOncePerSection` correctly asserts each\npersistence note appears exactly once. Model-level tests (focus cycle,\nshift+tab, profile cycling, edit/seeding) are untouched and remain valid since\nthey operate on the model, not the render. One caveat: `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget`\nis misnamed — it pins the line count at `23 + len(profileOptions)` = 28 as a\nregression guard against the old ~30, but it does **not** assert the actual\n24-row / 22-content-row budget the task required. It therefore passes while the\nreal height requirement fails. This should be fixed to assert the true budget\n(or the form compressed so it actually fits).\n\n## Security\n\nnone (render-only change; no filesystem, credential, or network surface touched).\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nBlockers before merge:\n1. The 24-row height budget must be met. At a standard 80×24 terminal the\n   Project settings section (Base branch, Job branch prefix — 2 of the 7\n   settings) and the footer are fully cut off, which the task explicitly\n   required to be visible. Either compress the render to fit the 22 content\n   rows (drop blank lines, merge/shorten the profile note and example lines,\n   tighten section separation — the analyst's own guidance prioritized these\n   over section separation) or otherwise resolve the overflow. The developer\n   should verify in a real `mg tui` at 24 rows and confirm the footer and\n   Project settings are visible.\n2. `TestSettingsRenderFitsHeightBudget` should assert the real budget (that the\n   render fits the 22 content rows available at a 24-row terminal), not merely\n   a fixed 28-line count, so the height requirement is actually guarded by a\n   test.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":71,"totalLines":71,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/verdict.md","time":{"start":1787920810622,"end":1787920810628}},"id":"prt_04862818a001mYK8WNZFGuC0DR","sessionID":"ses_fb79f1c04ffeYG6ohZOnXBocr5","messageID":"msg_0486260ac001qtFIeiZ9fWTiRz"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787920810686,"sessionID":"ses_fb79f1c04ffeYG6ohZOnXBocr5","part":{"id":"prt_04862737f0010hZq5qbhEakScL","messageID":"msg_0486260ac001qtFIeiZ9fWTiRz","sessionID":"ses_fb79f1c04ffeYG6ohZOnXBocr5","type":"text","text":"Confirmed. The developer made no code changes after the `NEEDS WORK` verdict. The two blockers from the prior review remain entirely unaddressed.\n\nLet me verify my line count math by re-examining the render output once more and finalize. Let me also double-check there isn't a scroll mechanism in Bubble Tea that would allow scrolling the settings content (the prior verdict claimed no scroll).\n\nFrom app.go `View()`, `stateSettings` returns `a.settingsView.render()` directly, wrapped only in `uiPaddingStyle`. There's no viewport/scroll — confirmed. Bubble Tea renders the returned string at the top of the screen; content beyond the terminal height is clipped by the terminal. So at 24 rows (22 content rows after padding), the render's 28 lines overflow.\n\nLet me now determine exactly which lines are cut. Content lines 1-22 visible (rows 2-23), line 23 at row 24 (last), lines 24-28 cut. So cut off: Base branch example (24), Job branch prefix field (25), Job branch prefix example (26), blank (27), footer (28). The Job branch prefix setting's input is off-screen and the save/cancel footer is gone.\n\nThis is a genuine, explicit-task-requirement failure. Both blockers from the prior verdict remain.\n\nLet me write the verdict.\n\n","time":{"start":1787920806783,"end":1787920810684}}}
